isIndecomposable -- tests whether a module or coherent sheaf is indecomposable
******************************************************************************

  * Usage: 
        isIndecomposable M
  * Inputs:
      * M, a *note module: (Macaulay2Doc)Module, or a *note coherent sheaf:
        (Varieties)CoherentSheaf,,
  * *note Optional inputs: (Macaulay2Doc)using functions with optional inputs,:
      * Strategy (missing documentation) => ..., default value null, 
      * Verbose (missing documentation) => ..., default value false, 
  * Outputs:
      * a *note Boolean value: (Macaulay2Doc)Boolean,, when the algorithm
        certifies decomposability or indecomposability
      * when the available tests are inconclusive

Description
===========

This function runs inexpensive indecomposability checks without invoking the
full decomposition algorithm. It returns false if it finds a splitting, true if
indecomposability is certified, and null otherwise.

As an example, we prove the indecomposability of the Horrocks–Mumford bundle
(see https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Horrocks–Mumford_bundle ) on $\PP^4$.

+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i1 : needsPackage "BGG"                                                      |
|                                                                             |
|o1 = BGG                                                                     |
|                                                                             |
|o1 : Package                                                                 |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i2 : S = ZZ/32003[x_0..x_4];                                                 |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i3 : E = ZZ/32003[e_0..e_4, SkewCommutative => true];                        |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i4 : alphad = map(E^5, E^{-2,-2}, transpose matrix{                          |
|             { e_1*e_4, -e_0*e_2, -e_1*e_3, -e_2*e_4,  e_0*e_3},             |
|             {-e_2*e_3, -e_3*e_4,  e_0*e_4, -e_0*e_1, -e_1*e_2}});           |
|                                                                             |
|             5      2                                                        |
|o4 : Matrix E  <-- E                                                         |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i5 : alpha = syz alphad;                                                     |
|                                                                             |
|             2      5                                                        |
|o5 : Matrix E  <-- E                                                         |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i6 : alphad = beilinson(alphad, S);                                          |
|                                                                             |
|o6 : Matrix                                                                  |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i7 : alpha = beilinson(alpha, S);                                            |
|                                                                             |
|o7 : Matrix                                                                  |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i8 : FHM = prune homology(alphad, alpha)                                     |
|                                                                             |
|o8 = cokernel {3} | -x_1x_4 x_3^2 0     x_1x_3  x_4^2 0      0     x_2x_3    |
|              {3} | x_2x_3  0     x_4^2 -x_0x_4 0     x_0x_3 x_1^2 0         |
|              {3} | 0       0     0     0       0     0      0     0         |
|              {3} | 0       0     0     0       0     0      0     x_1x_4    |
|              {4} | -x_0    -x_1  x_3   0       0     0      x_2   0         |
|              {4} | 0       -x_4  0     0       0     -x_1   0     0         |
|              {4} | 0       0     -x_2  0       0     0      0     -x_4      |
|              {4} | 0       0     0     -x_2    x_1   0      0     0         |
|              {4} | 0       0     0     0       -x_3  0      0     x_0       |
|              {4} | 0       0     0     0       0     x_2    0     0         |
|              {4} | 0       0     0     0       0     x_4    -x_3  -x_1      |
|              {4} | 0       0     0     0       0     0      0     0         |
|              {4} | 0       0     0     0       0     0      0     0         |
|              {4} | 0       0     0     0       0     0      0     0         |
