findProjectors -- construct projectors on a homogeneous module
**************************************************************

  * Usage: 
        findProjectors M
  * Inputs:
      * M, a *note module: (Macaulay2Doc)Module, or a *note coherent sheaf:
        (Varieties)CoherentSheaf,, expected to be homogeneous
  * *note Optional inputs: (Macaulay2Doc)using functions with optional inputs,:
      * Limit (missing documentation) => ..., default value null, 
      * Splitting
      * Strategy (missing documentation) => ..., default value 3, 
      * Tries (missing documentation) => ..., default value null, 
      * Verbose (missing documentation) => ..., default value false, 
  * Outputs:
      * a *note list: (Macaulay2Doc)List,, of endomorphisms that can be used to
        split $M$

Description
===========

This routine constructs projectors from a general degree-zero endomorphism and
its eigenvalues. It is the main splitting strategy for homogeneous modules.

See also
========

  * *note directSummands: directSummands, -- compute the direct summands of a
    module or coherent sheaf
  * *note generalEndomorphism: generalEndomorphism, -- construct a generic
    degree-zero endomorphism
  * *note findIdempotents: findIdempotents, -- construct idempotent
    endomorphisms

Ways to use findProjectors:
===========================

  * "findProjectors(Module)"

For the programmer
==================

The object *note findProjectors: findProjectors, is a *note method function
with options: (Macaulay2Doc)MethodFunctionWithOptions,.

