findIdempotents -- construct idempotent endomorphisms
*****************************************************

  * Usage: 
        findIdempotents M
  * Inputs:
      * M, a *note module: (Macaulay2Doc)Module, or a *note coherent sheaf:
        (Varieties)CoherentSheaf,,
  * *note Optional inputs: (Macaulay2Doc)using functions with optional inputs,:
      * Limit (missing documentation) => ..., default value null, 
      * Splitting
      * Strategy (missing documentation) => ..., default value 3, 
      * Tries (missing documentation) => ..., default value null, 
      * Verbose (missing documentation) => ..., default value false, 
  * Outputs:
      * a *note list: (Macaulay2Doc)List,, of idempotent endomorphisms of $M$
        suitable for splitting

Description
===========

This routine constructs nontrivial idempotents in the endomorphism algebra of a
module. When successful, those idempotents can be used to recover direct sum
decompositions. This is the main splitting strategy for modules over local
rings.

See also
========

  * *note directSummands: directSummands, -- compute the direct summands of a
    module or coherent sheaf
  * *note isIndecomposable: isIndecomposable, -- tests whether a module or
    coherent sheaf is indecomposable
  * *note generalEndomorphism: generalEndomorphism, -- construct a generic
    degree-zero endomorphism

Ways to use findIdempotents:
============================

  * "findIdempotents(Module)"

For the programmer
==================

The object *note findIdempotents: findIdempotents, is a *note method function
with options: (Macaulay2Doc)MethodFunctionWithOptions,.

