findSplitInclusion -- construct a split inclusion of one module into another
****************************************************************************

  * Usage: 
        findSplitInclusion(M, N)
  * Inputs:
      * M, a *note module: (Macaulay2Doc)Module,, 
      * N, a *note module: (Macaulay2Doc)Module,, 
  * *note Optional inputs: (Macaulay2Doc)using functions with optional inputs,:
      * Tries (missing documentation) => ..., default value 50, 
  * Outputs:
      * a *note matrix: (Macaulay2Doc)Matrix,, a split injection $M \to N$ when
        one is found
      * when no such map is found

Description
===========

This function performs a randomized search for maps $M \to N$ and $N \to M$
whose composition is an isomorphism of $M$.

See also
