generalEndomorphism -- construct a generic degree-zero endomorphism
*******************************************************************

  * Usage: 
        generalEndomorphism M
  * Inputs:
      * M, a *note module: (Macaulay2Doc)Module, or a *note coherent sheaf:
        (Varieties)CoherentSheaf,,
  * *note Optional inputs: (Macaulay2Doc)using functions with optional inputs,:
      * CoefficientRing (missing documentation) => ..., default value null, 
      * Density (missing documentation) => ..., default value 1, 
      * Height (missing documentation) => ..., default value 10, 
      * MaximalRank (missing documentation) => ..., default value false, 
      * UpperTriangular (missing documentation) => ..., default value false, 
  * Outputs:
      * a *note matrix: (Macaulay2Doc)Matrix, or a *note morphism of sheaves:
        (Varieties)SheafMap,,

Description
===========

This function forms a random linear combination of generators of the
degree-zero endomorphism space of $M$. It is used internally by the splitting
algorithms and can also be useful for experimentation.

See also
========

  * *note findProjectors: findProjectors, -- construct projectors on a
    homogeneous module
  * *note findIdempotents: findIdempotents, -- construct idempotent
    endomorphisms

