tallySummands -- tally a list of modules up to isomorphism
**********************************************************

  * Usage: 
        tallySummands L
  * Inputs:
      * L, a *note list: (Macaulay2Doc)List,, of modules or coherent sheaves
  * *note Optional inputs: (Macaulay2Doc)using functions with optional inputs,:
      * Homogeneous (missing documentation) => ..., default value true, 
      * Strategy (missing documentation) => ..., default value null, 
      * Strict (missing documentation) => ..., default value false, 
      * Tries (missing documentation) => ..., default value null, 
      * Verbose (missing documentation) => ..., default value false, 
  * Outputs:
      * a *note tally: (Macaulay2Doc)Tally,, whose keys are representatives of
        isomorphism classes

Description
===========

This function converts a list of summands into a tally modulo isomorphism.

+----------------------------------------------------+
|i1 : R = ZZ/101[x,y]/ideal(x^3, x^2*y^3, y^5);      |
+----------------------------------------------------+
|i2 : F = res(coker vars R, LengthLimit => 5)        |
|                                                    |
|      1      2      4      8      16      32        |
|o2 = R  <-- R  <-- R  <-- R  <-- R   <-- R          |
|                                                    |
|     0      1      2      3      4       5          |
|                                                    |
|o2 : Complex                                        |
+----------------------------------------------------+
|i3 : tallySummands summands coker F.dd_5            |
|                                                    |
|o3 = Tally{cokernel {7}  | x2   0 0  0 y4 0  | => 3}|
|                    {8}  | -48y x y3 0 0  0  |      |
|                    {10} | 0    0 0  y x  x2 |      |
|           cokernel {8} | x  0  y4 0   | => 2       |
|                    {8} | -y x2 0  xy3 |            |
|           cokernel {8} | y x | => 3                |
|                                                    |
|o3 : Tally                                          |
